<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="Read how the AC to DC calculator handles calculator inputs, editor authentication, local reports, sponsored banners, and hosting request information."><div class="shell page-intro legal"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} /><h1>Privacy policy</h1><div class="prose"><p>Updated 3 November 2026. This policy describes the prelaunch AC to DC site; the operator must review it before public launch.</p><h2>Calculator inputs</h2><p>Calculations run locally in your browser. The public calculator does not send input values to a server, save them in local storage, or require an account. Downloaded issue reports are generated on your device.</p><h2>Cookies, banners, and analytics</h2><p>The public calculator pages set no application cookies and include no analytics or third-party tracking scripts. If enabled by the operator, sponsored image/text banners are labeled and link to their destination websites. Following a reference or sponsored link takes you to an independently operated website with its own policies.</p><h2>Editorial accounts</h2><p>The private production dashboard verifies the approved editor’s email and password over HTTPS. It stores a salted password verifier and an encrypted signing key, and uses a secure, HttpOnly session cookie lasting up to eight hours. Original passwords are not stored. Login attempts are rate limited using request IP information. Editorial changes are stored as source files and commit history in the operator's GitHub repository. No visitor account is needed to use the calculator.</p><h2>Hosting requests</h2><p>The hosting provider receives request information such as IP address, requested URL, and browser headers to serve the website. Provider logging, security processing, and retention depend on the operator's account settings. Review <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for provider information.</p><h2>Contact information</h2><p>If you choose to email the operator or open a repository issue, the destination service processes what you submit. Avoid personal or sensitive information. See <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> for the configured channel.</p></div></div></Base>
